        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe plumbing is all correct and idiomatic \u2014 the `Owner` field + getters/setters, the `@Mapping(ignore = true)`, the schema column across all four dialects, the OpenAPI `readOnly` schema, and the YAML step insertion all match how the sibling warning flags (`bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, etc.) are done. The naming (`AssignCapacityWarning`) and Javadoc are consistent too.\n\nThe one structural problem: **`AssignCapacityWarning` re-scans the owner table to re-derive a count this pipeline already computes, duplicating both the scan and the capacity constant.**\n\nThis codebase has an established idiom for exactly this \"hard limit + soft warning off the same count\" situation, and this change doesn't follow it. Compare the daily-registration case:\n\n- `CountDailyRegistrations` does the `findAll()` scan once and publishes `Out<Integer> dailyRegistrationCount`.\n- `EnsureDailyRegistrationLimit` (the hard limit) reads `@Val Integer`.\n- `AssignBulkSignupWarning` (the warning) reads `@Val Integer`.\n- Its Javadoc even states the intent: both rules \"read the published value rather than re-scanning the table.\"\n\nThe city-capacity case now violates that same pattern:\n\n- `EnsureCityCapacity` scans `findAll()` and counts city matches (hard limit at 50).\n- `AssignCapacityWarning` scans `findAll()` **again** and counts city matches (warning at 40\u201349) \u2014 the identical case-insensitive loop.\n- `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` is now declared in **both** classes, so the limit lives in two places.\n\nConcrete fix, mirroring the daily-registration trio:\n\n1. Extract a `CountCityOwners` step that runs before `ensureCityCapacity`, does the city scan once, and publishes `Out<Integer> cityOwnerCount` (working off the DTO's city, as `EnsureCityCapacity` currently does).\n2. Change `EnsureCityCapacity` to read `@Val Integer cityOwnerCount` instead of scanning, keeping `CITY_CAPACITY` as the single owner of the hard limit (or hoist the constant to one shared home).\n3. Change `AssignCapacityWarning` to read `@Val Integer cityOwnerCount` and drop its own scan and its duplicate `CITY_CAPACITY`, keeping only `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD`.\n\nThis removes the second full-table scan, keeps the capacity limit defined once, and makes the new step read like the warning steps already in this pipeline."
